WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.025
Check yourself with two questions.

2
00:00:02.025 --> 00:00:05.294
First: a task's response
due date is tomorrow,

3
00:00:05.294 --> 00:00:08.200
and its action due date is in ten months.

4
00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:09.125
Which is right?

5
00:00:09.125 --> 00:00:10.800
The answer is b, both.

6
00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:14.662
The response window says how fast
the owner must pick the task up;

7
00:00:14.662 --> 00:00:17.650
the provider's date says
when the work must be done.

8
00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:21.637
They answer different questions, so
the kit keeps them in separate fields.

9
00:00:21.637 --> 00:00:25.587
Second: AWS closes its
security notification.

10
00:00:25.587 --> 00:00:26.875
What does the router do?

11
00:00:26.875 --> 00:00:28.087
The answer is c.

12
00:00:28.087 --> 00:00:31.490
It writes a close payload
that asks for the re-read,

13
00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:35.475
clause C4, and the task is resolved
on the agency's own check.

14
00:00:35.475 --> 00:00:39.425
The provider closing its notice
isn't the agency's work being done.

15
00:00:39.425 --> 00:00:41.852
The module page has three more questions,

16
00:00:41.852 --> 00:00:44.400
each linked to the
section that answers it.
